The portable C in the scenario move: what it is expected to show otherwise
than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/move.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 11 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: an error beeps, and the BIOS moves the screen up a row for the beep, with
the panels on it. What the program then puts back where its boxes were leaves
the fifth row of the Info panel on two rows or three, one under the other,
whole or beside what is left of a box. The rule of the Info's top knows the
panel once, where most of it shows, and not one row of it by itself: the
original has its count of free memory in that row, and the portable C has it
empty

